Description: DNS blocklists as FortiGate threat feeds
 forti-hole downloads DNS blocklists (hagezi, StevenBlack, your own lists),
 deduplicates them across sources and filtering tiers, and keeps them on a
 FortiGate as push-mode external threat feeds that its DNS filter profiles
 block. It checks the compiled set against the device's domain-entry limit
 and memory before writing, sends only what changed, and verifies on the
 device what it loaded.
 .
 It is never in the traffic path: a systemd user timer (shipped, never
 enabled) runs it twice a day. A failed download never empties a feed. It
 writes only feeds and DNS filter profiles carrying its own name prefix and
 ownership marker, and changes a firewall policy only when told to
 (`forti-hole attach`).
 .
 Device profiles and credentials are managed with `forti configure` from the
 forti-cli package; the command engine it shares with forti is compiled in.
